# ASSISTANT

This is a large test file. I can see the issue now - several TypeScript tests share the same workspace fixture. When `test_replace_function_basic` runs and modifies `main.ts`, even though it has a `finally` block, other tests running in parallel on the same workspace can see the modified file. The tests use `scope="class"` which means all tests in the class share the same workspace.

The key problem is that `test_replace_function_basic` changes the file, and even though it has a `finally` block, another test that runs in parallel (like `test_calls_outgoing` which depends on line 6 of main.ts) can see the modified version.

Let me look at one of the fixture files to understand what line 6 should look like:

